AB  - With the rapid advancement of Artificial Intelligence (AI), particularly the emergence of generative large language models (LLMs), AI technologies have been widely adopted across diverse sectors, significantly enhancing operational efficiency and transforming traditional workflows. However, integration of AI technologies into chemical engineering education remains constrained by students’ limited programming proficiency and the scarcity of labeled datasets, thereby limiting the effective implementation of data-driven methodologies in experimental teaching. To promote the digitalization and intelligent transformation of experimental education, a digitally enhanced reform of the heat of combustion measurement experiment was proposed to bridge the gap between traditional laboratory instruction and emerging AI technologies. The reform systematically reconstructs the entire experimental process, including pre-experiment conceptual preparation, standardized experimental operation, intelligent data analysis, and data-driven predictive modeling of heat of combustion and molecular structures. MLabs Pro, an interactive virtual simulation platform, was used for pre-laboratory training to help students grasp experimental principles and key operations, with guaranteed accuracy and safety. During data processing, students interacted with the Doubao AI assistant to generate Python-based analytical workflows which could lower the barrier to programming and minimize reliance on proprietary software. Furthermore, generative AI models were utilized to develop predictive data-driven models for the heat of combustion and molecular structures of various compounds. This reform integrates generative LLMs and neural network predictive modeling with traditional chemical experiments. It shifts students’ learning from operational practice toward data-driven exploration, while enhancing their ability in scientific reasoning, interdisciplinary application, and practical problem-solving. Meanwhile, hypothesis-oriented learning helps students better grasp abstract theories, exploring composition-structure-property correlations, and cultivate critical thinking skills.
